 "issue": 488,
 "issue_title": "load_all returns type='Biconvex' for a lens: the metadata blob overwrites the 'Lens' row marker",
 "issue_body": "Found while fixing #431. Not caused by that work, and verified identical on\n`master` at `adec854`.\n\n**Where:** `src/database.py` \u2014 `load_all`, both the lenses and the assemblies\npass.\n\n`load_all` tags each row before decoding it:\n\n```python\nlens[\"type\"] = \"Lens\"          # explicit row marker\n...\n_metadata_merge(lens, lens[\"metadata\"], ...)   # target.update(meta)\n```\n\n`_metadata_merge` flattens the stored blob over the row, and the blob has\nalways carried `Lens.to_dict()[\"type\"]`, which holds the **lens type**\n(`\"Biconvex\"`, `\"Meniscus\"`, ...), not the row marker. So the merge overwrites\nthe marker and every lens comes back as:\n\n```\n'type': 'Biconvex'\n```\n\n## Why it has not bitten anyone\n\n`LensStorage.load_lenses` dispatches on `type != \"OpticalSystem\"`, so the\nproduction path is unaffected \u2014 a lens whose type is `Biconvex` is still\ncorrectly treated as a Lens. The collision is only observable to code that\nfilters on the documented marker.\n\nIt already has bitten the test suite: `tests/test_database.py::_load_lenses`\nfilters `r.get(\"type\") == \"Lens\"` and therefore returns `[]` for every call.\nAny assertion built on it is passing vacuously rather than checking anything.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom src.database import DatabaseManager\nfrom src.lens import Lens\nimport tempfile\npath = tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix=\".db\", delete=False).name\nDatabaseManager(path).save_lens(Lens(name=\"X\").to_dict())\nprint(DatabaseManager(path).load_all()[0][\"type\"])   # 'Biconvex', not 'Lens'\n```\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nKeep the marker distinct from the payload. Either store the marker under a key\nthe blob cannot collide with (`row_type`, or reuse the absence of `elements`),\nor exclude `type` from the merge and expose the lens type under its own key\n(`lens_type`) in both `to_dict` and `from_dict`. The second is clearer but\ntouches the existing JSON interchange format, so it wants a migration note.\n\nWorth auditing every `type == \"Lens\"` / `type == \"OpticalSystem\"` comparison in\nthe codebase at the same time \u2014 the tests and the production code disagree\nabout what that field means, which is the actual hazard here.\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/488",
 "pr": 541,
 "pr_title": "fix(data): the row marker is row_type, not the lens type",
 "pr_body": "## Description\n\nfix(data): the row marker is `row_type`, not the lens type\n\n`DatabaseManager.load_all` tagged each row with a kind *before* decoding it:\n\n```python\nlens[\"type\"] = \"Lens\"          # explicit row marker\n...\nlens[\"metadata\"] = _metadata_merge(lens, lens.pop(\"metadata\", None), ...)\n```\n\n`_metadata_merge` merges the stored blob **flat** onto the same dict, and `Lens.to_dict()[\"type\"]` is the lens type (`\"Biconvex\"`, ...). The merge therefore overwrote the marker, and every lens row came back with `type: \"Biconvex\"`. Anything that filtered on `type == \"Lens\"` matched nothing \u2014 including the helper in `tests/test_database.py`, so **eleven assertions built on it had been passing vacuously**.\n\n### The fix\n\n- The marker now lives on its own key, **`row_type`** (`\"Lens\"` / `\"OpticalSystem\"`), and is set **after** the merge, so a stored blob cannot spoof it.\n- The payload keeps `type` as the model's own type; `Lens.from_dict` gets the lens type back instead of a marker.\n- `LensStorage.load_lenses` dispatched on `type` too and now dispatches on `row_type`. This also fixes an assembly row whose payload has no `type` key \u2014 the seed data writes those \u2014 being rebuilt as a `Lens`.\n- The issue's requested audit found **ten more test filters** keyed on the overloaded field (`test_metadata_resilience`, `test_stop_alignment`, `test_seed_data`, `test_coating`, `test_clear_aperture`, `test_e2e_persistence`, `test_metadata_persistence`, `test_assembly_lens_library_membership`); all use `row_type` now. The two migration tests and the `_load_lenses` helper are no longer no-ops.\n\n> Notably, two of those filters (`test_metadata_resilience`, `test_seed_data`) **broke under the fix before being migrated**: their assembly rows genuinely have no payload `type`, which is direct evidence that dispatching on `type` was relying on a coincidence.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [ ] Breaking change \u2014 `row_type` is a new key in `load_all()` rows; code that filtered on `type == \"Lens\"` was already broken (it matched nothing) and must use `row_type`\n\n## Related Issues\n\nCloses #488\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n\n- [x] 8 new tests (`TestLoadAllRowMarker`, `TestLensStorageUsesTheRowMarker` in `tests/test_database.py`), including a blob-spoof case (`Lens(metadata={\"row_type\": \"OpticalSystem\"})`) and a typeless-assembly dispatch case\n- [x] **Part-by-part reverts:**\n\n  | Reverted | Failures |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | lens marker back under `type` before the merge | 12 failures + 7 errors |\n  | assembly marker removed | 4 failures + 2 errors |\n  | marker set *before* the merge | 1 (blob spoof) |\n  | storage dispatch back on `type` | 1 (typeless assembly) |\n\n  The first revert's failure count is the measure of how much had been passing vacuously.\n- [x] Targeted: `test_database`, `test_database_migrations`, `test_metadata_resilience`, `test_metadata_persistence`, `test_assembly_lens_library_membership`, `test_stop_alignment`, `test_seed_data`, `test_coating`, `test_clear_aperture`, `test_e2e_persistence` \u2014 167 tests, OK\n- [x] Full suite: `Ran 2203 tests`, `FAILED (errors=6, skipped=34)` \u2014 the same six pre-existing `gui_flows` loader errors, no new failures\n- [x] `black --check` \u2014 250 files unchanged; `flake8` \u2014 byte-identical finding sets to master for both source files (the pre-existing `database.py` `E501` and `gui/storage.py` `E402`/`F401` are untouched)\n\n### Coverage\n\nLens row: marker present, `type` retains the real lens type (`Biconvex`, `Plano-Convex`); assembly row: marker present; blob cannot spoof the marker; a row with no blob still gets a marker; `LensStorage` returns a `Lens` with its `lens_type` intact; returns an `OpticalSystem` for a normal assembly and for a typeless one.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] My code follows the style guidelines\n- [x] I have performed a self-review\n- [x] I have commented my code, particularly in hard-to-understand areas\n- [x] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation (`load_all` docstring documents `row_type`)\n- [ ] My changes generate no new warnings\n- [x] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective\n- [x] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes\n",
